Upstream adds variant globally (a never-strip name that is also a corpus
functional_params name): Risky fails. So does psc, a corpus functional name
only, and a name listed only in testdata/golden/risky-params.txt.
-- ops --
jappend rules/brave/clean-urls.json [{"include": "*://*/*"}, "params"] "variant"
relock
run Risky
fail Risky: new global pair (global, variant)
jremove rules/brave/clean-urls.json [{"include": "*://*/*"}, "params"] "variant"
jappend rules/brave/clean-urls.json [{"include": "*://*/*"}, "params"] "psc"
relock
run Risky
fail Risky: new global pair (global, psc): psc is a risky name (corpus functional_params)
jremove rules/brave/clean-urls.json [{"include": "*://*/*"}, "params"] "psc"
jappend rules/brave/clean-urls.json [{"include": "*://*/*"}, "params"] "fixture_risky"
